Join us for our very first Zig Day in Zurich on Saturday, November 14th at ZHAW Europaallee.

No matter if you are new to Zig or are already experienced, the goal is to come and meet other Zig users, work on something together, and share what you learn.

PLEASE RSVP ON [Luma](https://luma.com/azc64bip) because seats are limited.

What to bring:

 * A laptop and/or other hardware
 * An idea for something to work on that is open to collaboration from others,
 * or something you want to learn together.
 * OR if you’re fresh out of ideas, come with a willingness to help out a stranger with theirs!

 What to expect:

| time          | activity                                  |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| 09:30 - 10:00 | gathering & chat                          |
| 10:00 - 10:30 | explain projects, form groups, get set up |
| 10:30 - 12:30 | coding & learning                         |
| 12:30 - 14:00 | lunch break                               |
| 14:00 - 14:30 | reconvene & status update                 |
| 14:30 - 16:30 | coding & learning                         |
| 16:30 - 17:00 | show & tell                               |

PLEASE RSVP ON [Luma](https://luma.com/azc64bip) because seats are limited.
